## Introduction
Metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) have now acquired a prominent position in the literature owing to their ability to form porous extended networks, with record breaking surface areas1, low crystal density 2, and their potential in practical applications such as gas storage and separation3–5. The inherent tunability of these versatile crystal structures make them an ideal playground to obtain a fundamental understanding of how system
